From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:19:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 188/342] meson_mali: growable tile heaps

A heap buffer (MALI_BO_FLAG_HEAP, the GP's tile heap) now reserves GPU
addresses for its whole size but starts with 64 KiB of memory. When the
GP runs out (PLBU_OUT_OF_MEM), the job thread doubles the heap, maps the
new pages after the old, and the GP goes on from where its memory ended.
A heap's area isn't cloneable, and its lines aren't cleaned for jobs:
the CPU never touches it after making it.

With lima's fixed 1 MiB heaps, busy frames failed (GP error 0x4) and the
PP jobs after them failed too. The libdrm stand-in now says version 1.1,
so lima makes heap buffers of 16 MiB.

Also: a buffer whose mapping fails gives its GPU addresses back; the KDL
"mali" command counts heap growths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
